      "text": "Outcome: resolve_altitude. Tariq, the operation is not ready for release because the planned altitude is above the Part 107 limit.\n\n- **Altitude (fails):** The highest waypoint was checked against the terrain model. It gives a maximum planned altitude of 500 ft AGL. That exceeds the 400 ft AGL limit in 14 CFR 107.51(b). The evidence does not mention any structure-proximity exception. The flight plan needs to be revised to stay at or below 400 ft AGL before release.\n- **Pilot (passes):** Mei Mensah holds a valid remote pilot certificate and has current aeronautical knowledge.\n- **Airspace (passes):** The location is uncontrolled Class G airspace, so no controlled-airspace authorization is needed.\n- **Visibility (passes):** Forecast flight visibility is 5 statute miles, cross-checked against the nearest observations. The minimum is 3.\n- **Cloud clearance (passes):** Planned separation meets the 500 ft below / 2,000 ft horizontal minimums.\n- **Speed (passes):** Maximum planned groundspeed is 80 mph, under the 100 mph (87 knot) limit.",
